think Equinox 2's deliverable is the starter module + its witness a newcomer builds in their first hour — the smallest thing that still carries the whole TAME discipline; design-season discipline says design not build, so I made it a checkable contract with a validated reference
think to keep it measured (like Equinox 1's anchor line), I built the reference in a SCRATCH tree — greet.rye (a bounded greeting) + greet_witness.rish — and ran both GREEN, so the contract carries a proven shape rather than proposed code; the development season types it into the repository
obs greet.rye meets the SLC Rye Definition of Done in one screen: opening triad (std·assert·print), a named bound (max_name), an invariant assert at each edge with its // invariant: reason, a selftest that proves by comparison (hello, grain!), a GREEN line; no @memcpy (byte loops)
obs greet_witness.rish is the discipline at the outside: check .ok before trusting output, assert the GREEN line and one named claim (proven to fit its buffer); reads st.err since std.debug.print writes to stderr
obs acceptance line measured on metal in scratch 20260811.163927: "GREEN: greet — your first Grain module builds, bounds its input, and greets by proof." — the first hour is done when a newcomer's own greet builds and prints it and their own witness greens
obs the design season stays design: the tracked artifact is the contract (reference inline as code blocks); the build was throwaway in scratch, so no new tracked binary or half-built module; marked Equinox 2 landed in the plan; living_docs_lint GREEN
loom module=greet build=GREEN(scratch) witness=greet_witness selftest=GREEN
file active-designing/20260811-163927_acme-dx-first-hour-witness-contract.md the contract — greet.rye + greet_witness.rish reference inline, acceptance line, SLC done
file expanding-prompts/20260811-145659_acme-dx-design-season.md Equinox 2 marked landed with a pointer
recommend check-in (Claude) — two of the design season's four equinoxes are checkable contracts now (onboarding path · first-hour witness), each validated on metal; Equinox 3 (the interfaces surface — the API/CLI/desk shape a developer composes their own module against) is the next design lap. That, or the coupled SLC-2a/sub-lap relabel on a qemu-capable bench, are the open doors. Rest is Keaton's to take
